WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.520
What do we knlow about X-Force?

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.100
We will be known as X-Force."

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.120
"Isn't that a little derivative?"

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.580
Well, besides that.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.190
We know Drew Goddard is writing and directing,
and he plans to focus on Deadpool, Cable,

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:15.840
and Domino.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.980
There was already plenty of stuff up in the
air before the Disney-Fox merger, but now

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.560
things are even more muddled.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.560
But there's no reason to lose hope just yet.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.820
No matter what Disney plans to do with our
favorite merc-with-a-mouth, all signs point

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.420
toward Goddard, Ryan Reynolds, and the rest
giving us at least one great movie featuring

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:32.920
X-Force.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.340
Here's a look at all the X-Force rumors and
spoilers that have leaked so far.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.120
Rated R

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.899
If there's one consensus about X-Force, it's
that just about everyone wants it to be rated

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.280
R. Ryan Reynolds told Collider he thinks that'll
be the case, but it's too soon to say with

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.440
certainty, telling them,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.480
"My sort of wild guess would be that it would
be an R-rated movie, but again, right now

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.620
we're just assembling the troops to figure
out what story we would tell."

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.340
Even the writers not working on X-Force are
sure we'll get an R rating.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.320
Deadpool 2 writer Rhett Reese told CBR that
X-Force will almost definitely be rated R.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.780
You might wanna look away from this.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.340
Now this little piggy went to..."

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.740
Back from the dead

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.250
One of Deadpool 2's most hilariously unexpected
scenes gave us the very messy deaths of most

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.080
of the original X-Force's lineup.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.680
Although, by the end of the film, one lucky
member did get resurrected from Deadpool's

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.980
post-credits time-hopping.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.420
But even though Deadpool brought Peter back
from the dead, it's unclear if the rest of

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.260
X-Force was so lucky.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.140
But Phillip Tan, who played Shatterstar in
Deadpool 2, says he will absolutely be returning

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.140
for X-Force.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.900
Speaking to Syfy, Tan predicted,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.660
"You're going to see more of my character
in the X-Force film."

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.120
Tan added that he's received a lot great fan
reaction from his death in Deadpool 2, and

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.680
he hopes the rest of the original doomed lineup
will be returning too.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.970
Shatterstar might have a loophole not available
to the rest of the others: Deadpool 2 stayed

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.000
at least partly faithful to the character's
origin in the comics.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.320
"So where are you from?"

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.640
"Planet Mojoworld?"

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.520
"So, you're an alien?

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.460
How does that help us?"

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.720
That alien origin could help by bringing Shatterstar
back for X-Force.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.660
Mister Sinister

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.260
Movieweb thinks there's a good chance the
X-Force movie may introduce us to Mister Sinister,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.700
whose introduction was originally planned
for Logan before director James Mangold decided

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.400
to cut him.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.800
In the comics, Mister Sinister's birth name
is Nathaniel Essex, and that name has been

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.540
popping up throughout the X movies.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.000
In X-Men: Apocalypse, men from something called
"Essex Corp" were shown collecting Logan's

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.500
blood.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.440
Essex is also the name of the school that
tortured Russell and other mutant students

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.280
in Deadpool 2.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.160
It's also worth noting that the headmaster
of the Essex School is never given a proper

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.480
name, referred to in the credits only as "The
Headmaster."

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.040
It could be that "The Headmaster" has a comeback
in store, despite his fatal ending in Deadpool

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.540
2.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.600
"The day of reckoning is here!"

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.740
If he were secretly Mister Sinister, that
would hardly matter.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.360
The villain has survived far worse.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.720
Free-spirited Deadpool

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.380
The Deadpool movies featured Wade Wilson in
a long-term relationship with Vanessa, but

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.170
in the comics, his sexuality goes far beyond
heterosexual.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:13.260
Longtime Deadpool comic book writer Gerry
Duggan says the Merc with a Mouth is, quote,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.890
"ready and willing to do anything with a pulse."

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:20.360
He's flirted with heroes like Thor and Spider-Man
in the comics, and we saw a little bit of

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.400
this with Wade's fixation on Colossus in Deadpool
2.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:32.420
Ryan Reynolds has been clear that he wants
to explore Deadpool's pansexuality.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:37.440
At the 2018 San Diego Comic-Con, he said one
of the reasons he loves working on Deadpool

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:42.640
is that they can break the usual superhero
boundaries, adding that LGBTQ representation

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.760
is something he wants represented more in
superhero movies, specifically through Wade.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.100
Since all the unanswered questions posed by
the Disney-Fox merger mean that X-Force could

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:56.060
very well be Reynolds' last crack at the character,
it may be do-or-die time for Deadpool to demonstrate

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.800
his romantic fluidity on screen.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.500
A post-merger prognosis

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.760
It's a strange time to be a part of a Marvel
franchise in Fox's stable, and with the Disney-Fox

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.510
merger official, fans are wondering about
the future of all things X.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.580
If Disney proves unwilling to be the home
of R-rated superhero movies, then that would

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.539
likely mean the end of the Deadpool movie
franchise, and subsequently, that X-Force

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.360
would be a waste of time and resources.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.960
We'll just have to wait and see if Deadpool
can survive an MCU merger in all his foul-mouthed,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.960
violent glory.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.980
"Oh, it's so hard to go.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.620
I just love being around you guys so much.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.080
So, so much."

